# 3D Visualization Patterns

## Three.js Architecture
Main component: [src/visuals/components/Visual3D.tsx](mdc:src/visuals/components/Visual3D.tsx)
- Scene management with sphere and backdrop meshes
- Audio-reactive geometry deformation
- HDR environment mapping with EXR textures
- Post-processing pipeline with bloom effects

## Shader System
Sphere shader: [src/visuals/shaders/sphere-shader.ts](mdc:src/visuals/shaders/sphere-shader.ts) - Vertex displacement from audio
Backdrop shader: [src/visuals/shaders/backdrop-shader.ts](mdc:src/visuals/shaders/backdrop-shader.ts) - Gradient background

## Audio-Reactive Animation Patterns
```typescript
// Real-time uniform updates from audio analysis
uniforms.time.value = performance.now() / 1000;
uniforms.audioData.value = new Float32Array(analyser.frequencyData);
uniforms.amplitude.value = analyser.getAverageAmplitude();
```

## Performance Optimization
- Target 60fps rendering
- Efficient geometry with icosahedron subdivision  
- Optimized shader compilation and uniform updates
- Memory-conscious texture and buffer management

## Rendering Pipeline
1. Audio Analysis → Frequency data extraction
2. Shader Uniforms → Real-time parameter updates  
3. Vertex Displacement → Audio-reactive deformation
4. Post-Processing → Bloom effects and anti-aliasing
5. WebGL Output → 60fps animation loop

## Integration Requirements
- Synchronization with audio input/output streams
- No interference with real-time audio processing
- Graceful degradation for low-performance devices
- Proper cleanup of WebGL resources